+### Flaky-test triage (added 2026-10-27)
+
+Before any hypothesis, the Investigator re-runs the target three times in isolation and, if it
+never fails there, once with the rest of its file. The target is classified as **deterministic**,
+**intermittent** (fails some isolated runs), **order-dependent** (passes alone, fails with its
+neighbours: shared state leaking between tests) or **unknown**. The classification goes into the
+hypothesis prompt, the evidence report and the verifier's re-run policy.
+
+## Modes
+
+The same orchestrator, sandbox, provider and verifier run three systems, so the benchmark compares
+methods rather than plumbing:
+
+| Mode | What the model gets | Claims a fix when |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `baseline` · Baseline A | one repair call | it produced a patch (the verifier only measures it) |
+| `iterative` · Baseline C | an edit → run tests → see results loop, with the same call budget as FORGE-0 (`1 + max_experiment_rounds + max_repair_attempts`) and the full test deltas of every earlier attempt | the verifier accepts a patch |
+| `forge` · FORGE-0 | hypotheses → experiments → belief updates → repair | the verifier accepts a patch |
+
+Baseline C is the fair comparison: it is how coding agents work today.
+
